  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are climbing a staircase with N stairs. Each time you can either climb 1 or 2 steps. Calculate in how many distinct ways can you climb to the top.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains TTT - the number of test cases\nEach test case contains a single integer NNN - the number of stairs\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, output a single integer - the number of ways to climb NNN stairs",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "0≤N≤10000 \\leq N \\leq 10000≤N≤1000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n3\n4",
        "output": "2\n3\n5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: N = 2\nWay 1: 1 step + 1 step \nWay 2: 2 steps \nTotal ways = 2\nTest Case 2: N = 3\nWay 1: 1 step + 1 step + 1 step \nWay 2: 1 step + 2 steps \nWay 3: 2 steps + 1 step \nTotal ways = 3\nTest Case 3: N = 4\nWay 1: 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 \nWay 2: 1 + 1 + 2 \nWay 3: 1 + 2 + 1 \nWay 4: 2 + 1 + 1 \nWay 5: 2 + 2 \nTotal ways = 5"
      }
    ]
  },
